  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: ResCoordDisc 2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "At your cancer center, a colleague introduces you to a support group
    volunteer who has questions about early research for colorectal cancer. You explain
    that most of your work as the research coordinator in the early clinical research
    is to help make sure discoveries made in the lab can later be tested safely in
    humans. She responds, \u201CI see\u2026 So, it sounds like research coordinators
    are the ones creating and testing new drug ideas in the lab to make sure they\u2019re
    safe for people.\u201D\n\nIs this true or false?"
  explanation: "Research coordinators don\u2019t design or test new drugs themselves.
    Their main role is to support the research process \u2014 such as organizing
    data, tracking samples, and/or ensuring compliance with ethical and regulatory
    standards \u2014 not conducting lab-based experiments. By managing these behind-the-scenes
    tasks, they help researchers focus on the discovery work happening in the lab."
  correctAnswer: False
  incorrectAnswer1: True
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Research Coordinator
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Discovery
